{{!
    @template tool_vae/setup_page

    The page "Mise en route" (lot S1), below its heading: the steps of the setup, in their order.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\setup_page. The template holds no logic: the right
    that a link asks is checked before, and a step gets either its link or the name of its screen and the right it asks.
    Every value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * intro - string, the sentence above the steps
    * steps - array of steps, each with:
        * key - string, the key of the step, part of the id of its item
        * title - string, the title of the step
        * state - string, its state in words
        * details - array of strings, its sentences
        * guide - string, the parts of the installation guide it refers to
        * link - false, or an object {url, label}: the link to the screen of the step
        * needs - false, or a string: the name of the screen and the right it asks
    * footer - string, the sentence below the steps

    Example context (json):
    {
        "intro": "The steps of putting the plugin into service, in the order of the installation guide. This page changes nothing.",
        "steps": [
            {
                "key": "competencies",
                "title": "Competencies enabled",
                "state": "Done",
                "details": [],
                "guide": "Installation guide, part 4.",
                "link": {
                    "url": "https://example.com/admin/settings.php?section=optionalsubsystems",
                    "label": "Advanced features"
                },
                "needs": false
            },
            {
                "key": "cron",
                "title": "Cron running",
                "state": "To do",
                "details": ["The cron has never run."],
                "guide": "Installation guide, part 4.",
                "link": false,
                "needs": "Screen \"Scheduled tasks\": it needs the right moodle/site:config, which you do not have."
            }
        ],
        "footer": "The plugin does not know who holds a role nor which cohorts are attached: this is done in Moodle."
    }
}}
<p>{{intro}}</p>
<ol class="tool-vae-setup">
    {{#steps}}
    <li id="tool-vae-setup-{{key}}" class="mb-3"><strong>{{title}}</strong> <span class="tool-vae-setup-state">{{state}}</span>
        {{#details}}
        <p class="mb-0">{{.}}</p>
        {{/details}}
        <p class="mb-0 small text-muted">{{guide}}</p>
        {{#link}}
        <p class="mb-0"><a href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a></p>
        {{/link}}
        {{#needs}}
        <p class="mb-0">{{needs}}</p>
        {{/needs}}
    </li>
    {{/steps}}
</ol>
<p class="text-muted">{{footer}}</p>
